WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.070
A bouncing ball repeats its
motion, again and again.

2
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:06.140
So does a mass on a spring.

3
00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:09.060
Only one of them is
simple harmonic motion.

4
00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:11.600
Pull the mass aside and let go.

5
00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:14.530
At each end, the spring's
force is biggest,

6
00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.480
yet the mass is still.

7
00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:19.790
In the middle, there is
no overall force at all.

8
00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:22.890
And that is exactly
where it moves fastest.

9
00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:24.000
Why there?

10
00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:29.070
In this mission, you'll find the one
condition that makes a motion simple harmonic.

11
00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:31.190
Then you'll stack graphs of displacement,

12
00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:35.510
velocity and acceleration, and
read each one from another.

13
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:40.850
Your mission: explain why the mass moves
fastest where no overall force acts on

14
00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:41.250
it.
